+# Notes from your asks
+
+Rules, preferences and ideas you said about this module that are not work, one line each, with a link to your words. Written by `node Server/UndoneToTasks.mjs --notes --apply` from the sort pass over the undone asks ([crack 2](/framework/core/Task/doc/cracks.md)).
+
+- Tinted, darkened and lightened primary variants go off-brand and need contrast checks, so they are candidates to drop. ([your words](/framework/ai/sessions/f155ecbd-2911-4f55-bc4c-c1cf9d7b7026/?tab=coverage#p3908), 2026-10-13)
+- The primary background colour stays off for now, unless solid examples that work well turn up. ([your words](/framework/ai/sessions/f155ecbd-2911-4f55-bc4c-c1cf9d7b7026/?tab=coverage#p3908), 2026-10-13)
+- The primary background does not go on every screen or on many cards. ([your words](/framework/ai/sessions/f155ecbd-2911-4f55-bc4c-c1cf9d7b7026/?tab=coverage#p3908), 2026-10-13)
+- The primary is a minimal accent, never a bold splash, and colour use stays minimal. ([your words](/framework/ai/sessions/f155ecbd-2911-4f55-bc4c-c1cf9d7b7026/?tab=coverage#p3908), 2026-10-13)
+- Progress bars in the primary's orange-red can read as an error, so using the primary there needs weighing first. ([your words](/framework/ai/sessions/f155ecbd-2911-4f55-bc4c-c1cf9d7b7026/?tab=coverage#p3908), 2026-10-13)
+- The site uses one primary hue and introduces no other accent colours. ([your words](/framework/ai/sessions/f155ecbd-2911-4f55-bc4c-c1cf9d7b7026/?tab=coverage#p3908), 2026-10-13)
+- Stepping between dark surfaces with light text is preferred over returning to a light surface. ([your words](/framework/ai/sessions/f155ecbd-2911-4f55-bc4c-c1cf9d7b7026/?tab=coverage#p3908), 2026-10-13)
+- Primary is not used as a background fill until solid examples are nailed down. ([your words](/framework/ai/sessions/f155ecbd-2911-4f55-bc4c-c1cf9d7b7026/?tab=coverage#p1251), 2026-10-13)
+- The primary background is for rare moments, never the background of every screen or many cards. ([your words](/framework/ai/sessions/f155ecbd-2911-4f55-bc4c-c1cf9d7b7026/?tab=coverage#p1251), 2026-10-13)
+- Keep colour minimal: the primary is a bold accent, not a fill. ([your words](/framework/ai/sessions/f155ecbd-2911-4f55-bc4c-c1cf9d7b7026/?tab=coverage#p1251), 2026-10-13)
+- Use the orange-red primary sparingly, for example on progress bars, since it can read as an error colour. ([your words](/framework/ai/sessions/f155ecbd-2911-4f55-bc4c-c1cf9d7b7026/?tab=coverage#p1251), 2026-10-13)
+- Stick to the one primary hue and add no other colours. ([your words](/framework/ai/sessions/f155ecbd-2911-4f55-bc4c-c1cf9d7b7026/?tab=coverage#p1251), 2026-10-13)
+- The shaded primary colour is for places where contrast suits it, not a default fill. ([your words](/framework/ai/sessions/f155ecbd-2911-4f55-bc4c-c1cf9d7b7026/?tab=coverage#p3786), 2026-10-13)
+- Colour variants are an optional extra UI style, explored only if time allows. ([your words](/framework/ai/sessions/f155ecbd-2911-4f55-bc4c-c1cf9d7b7026/?tab=coverage#p3786), 2026-10-13)
