+# Notes from your asks
+
+Rules, preferences and ideas you said about this module that are not work, one line each, with a link to your words. Written by `node Server/UndoneToTasks.mjs --notes --apply` from the sort pass over the undone asks ([crack 2](/framework/core/Task/doc/cracks.md)).
+
+- Each response is summarised on the relevant Figma page, not repeated in chat. ([your words](/framework/ai/sessions/f155ecbd-2911-4f55-bc4c-c1cf9d7b7026/?tab=coverage#p2665), 2026-10-13)
+- Icons are FIXED width in Figma, so every glyph keeps its own box in a row, and a frame is added only for a click target or a grid of equal slots. ([your words](/framework/ai/sessions/f155ecbd-2911-4f55-bc4c-c1cf9d7b7026/?tab=coverage#p4962), 2026-10-13)
+- The full permutation stack exists only to make every variation visible, not to pick one. ([your words](/framework/ai/sessions/f155ecbd-2911-4f55-bc4c-c1cf9d7b7026/?tab=coverage#p4683), 2026-10-13)
+- The palette page is one palette component system: three solid bases, each with a fixed set of approved tints. ([your words](/framework/ai/sessions/f155ecbd-2911-4f55-bc4c-c1cf9d7b7026/?tab=coverage#p4607), 2026-10-13)
+- A palette master edit must reach all four duplicates, so each one stays an instance of the master. ([your words](/framework/ai/sessions/f155ecbd-2911-4f55-bc4c-c1cf9d7b7026/?tab=coverage#p4607), 2026-10-13)
+- Show all four permutations only where colour stacking and contrast need observing, not on every card. ([your words](/framework/ai/sessions/f155ecbd-2911-4f55-bc4c-c1cf9d7b7026/?tab=coverage#p4607), 2026-10-13)
+- Results go into the Figma file itself, not only into chat. ([your words](/framework/ai/sessions/f155ecbd-2911-4f55-bc4c-c1cf9d7b7026/?tab=coverage#p1652), 2026-10-13)
+- Figma work is built from reusable components and slots, not from one-off unique designs. ([your words](/framework/ai/sessions/f155ecbd-2911-4f55-bc4c-c1cf9d7b7026/?tab=coverage#p647), 2026-10-12)
